radeonsi without LLVM's AMDGPU target

radeonsi compiles its shaders with ACO, Mesa's own compiler for AMD GPUs,
when it is built with -Damd-use-llvm=false.  Mesa's build still asks
LLVM for its AMDGPU target whenever radeonsi is built, and fails when
LLVM has none (bunix's LLVM is built for AArch64 and X86 only: base.nix).
Asked only when LLVM is what radeonsi compiles with, as the line after
it already has it for the version of LLVM.

Mesa built with -Dllvm=disabled builds radeonsi with ACO alone; this is
that, with LLVM there for the other drivers.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1961,7 +1961,7 @@
 
 llvm_modules = ['bitwriter', 'engine', 'mcdisassembler', 'core', 'executionengine', 'scalaropts', 'transformutils', 'instcombine']
 llvm_optional_modules = ['coroutines']
-if with_amd_vk or with_gallium_radeonsi
+if (with_amd_vk or with_gallium_radeonsi) and amd_with_llvm
   llvm_modules += ['amdgpu', 'bitreader', 'ipo']
 endif
 if with_clc
